  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jack Fruit from Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fiber Foods offers dried  jackfruit fibers from East Africa to the vegetarian food industry in the Netherlands, who use the dried jackfruit as a natural fiber to make their vegetarian products healthier and tastier. Currently they use textured soy bean or peas, which gives the balls or burgers a sticky bite and on top of that the texturization of soybean is an energy draining process. Fiber Foods has built an entire value chain in East Africa, where the jackfruit is harvested and processed with the aim to create opportunities for women. The jack fruit were not Via a pre-financing loan Fiber Foods is able to advance the production of 3 containers of dried jackfruit. One container holds 7500 KG of dried jackfruit that is dried in both Uganda and Kenya out of 100,000 KG of jackfruit. This jackfruit is harvested twice a week with a group of more than a 1000 farmers. Instead of 8 containers of pasteurised jackfruit (in a brine) Fiber Foods ships only 1 container, leading to a smaller footprint than regular jackfruit.</narrative>
  </description>
